<title>USA: Strong cold front to push through Argentina.</title>
<headline>Strong cold front to push through Argentina.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strong cold front will move northeastward through Argentina Tuesday and into the central countries of South America and southern Brazil Wednesday, accompanied by showers forecaster, Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Much cooler air will push into Argentina behind this front.</p>
<p>Northern South America remains seasonable with widely scattered thundershowers on a daily basis.</p>
